        "id": 1329040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-22T16:13:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PD_GET_HEADER_SOP is not a part of PD spec, it isn\u0027t implemented on TCPMv1 and doesn\u0027t get stuffed with message type being transmitted. So, using PD_GET_HEADER_SOP will always return 0 irrespective of message type.\n\nIn case of TCPMv1, the type of messages is tracked with CABLE_FLAGS_SOP_PRIME_ENABLE, CABLE_FLAGS_SOP_PRIME_PRIME_ENABLE flags\n\nSo yes, the incoming message is checked with status of cable flags",
      "parentUuid": "c7593de3_57430263",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 785,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 785,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "841aee40709b8ba64e83161181726935f84e108d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cc7cbe72_1c4a7bfa",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 785,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-04-22T17:58:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When CONFIG_USB_PD_DECODE_SOP is enabled or TCPC_FLAGS_TCPCI_REV2_0 is defined by tcpc_config[], then the received header will have frame type added to bits 31:28.  See tcpci_tcpm_get_message_raw(), which is shared by TCPMv1 and TCPMv2.\n\nBecause the CABLE flags are only set if CONFIG_USB_PD_DECODE_SOP, the frame type should also be available for these code paths.\n\nThere are only 3 TCPC drivers that don\u0027t use tcpci_tcpm_get_message_raw().  I\u0027m looking at those data sheets to see if they provide a register to read the frame type.\n\nI think this can be cleaned up in CL:2159592 instead of here.",
      "parentUuid": "6b8674a6_f2996712",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 785,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 785,
        "endChar": 37
